Looking at the problem: I need to determine whether there exists $f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ satisfying (1) surjective, (2) everywhere discontinuous, (3) $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq f(\mathbb{I})$, (4) $f(\mathbb{Q})\subset\mathbb{I}$.

**Answer leak check:** The problem statement contains no solutions, hints, or formalization notes. Proceeding.

